"The functions B<asprintf>()  and B<vasprintf>()  are analogs of "
"B<sprintf>(3)  and B<vsprintf>(3), except that they allocate a string large "
"enough to hold the output including the terminating null byte "
"(\\[aq]\\[rs]0\\[aq]), and return a pointer to it via the first argument.  "
"This pointer should be passed to B<free>(3)  to release the allocated "
"storage when it is no longer needed."
msgstr ""
"B<asprintf>()  関数と B<vasprintf>()  関数とは、それぞれ B<sprintf>(3)  関数"
"と B<vsprintf>(3)  関数とに似ているが、 出力文字列を (終端のヌルバイト "
