"When I<flags> contain the B<AT_HANDLE_FID> (since Linux 6.5)  flag, the "
"caller indicates that the returned I<file_handle> is needed to identify the "
"filesystem object, and not for opening the file later, so it should be "
"expected that a subsequent call to B<open_by_handle_at>()  with the returned "
"I<file_handle> may fail."
