#: build/C/man2/open_by_handle_at.2:167
msgid ""
"When I<flags> contain the B<AT_HANDLE_MNT_ID_UNIQUE> (since Linux 6.12)  "
"flag, the caller indicates that the width of the I<mount_id> buffer is at "
"least 64 bits, and then the mount id returned in that buffer is the unique "
"mount id as the one returned by B<statx>(2)  with the B<STATX_MNT_ID_UNIQUE> "
"flag."
msgstr ""

#.  commit a20853ab8296d4a8754482cb5e9adde8ab426a25
#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/open_by_handle_at.2:190
msgid ""
"When I<flags> contain the B<AT_HANDLE_CONNECTABLE> (since Linux 6.13)  flag, "
"the caller indicates that the returned I<file_handle> is needed to open a "
"file with known path later, so it should be expected that a subsequent call "
"to B<open_by_handle_at>()  with the returned I<file_handle> may fail if the "
"file was moved, but otherwise, the path of the opened file is expected to be "
"visible from the I</proc/>pidI</fd/>* magic link.  This flag can not be used "
"in combination with the flags B<AT_HANDLE_FID> and/or B<AT_EMPTY_PATH>."
msgstr ""

